    Bug 1858157 - Fix nsMailboxUrl::GetMsgHdrForKey(). r=BenC,mkmelin

    This function has to use an absolute path to open the database to get the message header from, and this now only works if the database was previously opened from its nsIMsgFolder and could be retrieved from the cache. If this is not the case, the call in nsMailboxProtocol::Initialize() will fail and the underlying mbox file will be treated like a single .eml file.

    This patch changes nsMailboxUrl::GetMsgHdrForKey() to access the database cache directly first. If this fails, all accounts will be searched for an nsIMsgFolder that matches the absolute path from the `mailbox:` URI to be able to call nsMsgDBService::OpenFolderDB(). If no nsIMsgFolder could be found, the caller nsMailboxProtocol::Initialize() will receive `nullptr` and treat the URI as possibly pointing to an .EML file.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D228606

